Once you get to the late game, you do not need optimal damage.  Dual
wielding Mjollnir and a silver foo may not be as good as Grayswandir
and a silver foo, but it will work well enough to beat up practically
anything.  In contrast, in the time between when you would grab
Mjollnir and Greyswandir, going for the former is the difference
between easily beating up most enemies and having trouble with them.
Oh, and later on shock damage seems to work well against most enemies
that are not seared by silver, including elementals.

For comparison, my only ascension used Mjollnir and a non-silver
dagger for the last 2/3s of the game.  It was good enough.


